.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# `.env` alone missed the duplicates an editor or Explorer leaves behind
# (`.env copy`, `.env.bak`, `.env - Copy (2)`), each of which holds the same
# live credentials as the original while being perfectly stageable.
.env*
# ...except the committed template, which is the whole point of the pattern.
!.env.example
dev.db
*.db
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
